# Domains to route through the proxy (for ipset / selective routing)
# Used by `selective` mode, which is the shipped default (PROXY_MODE in
# config.sh.example).
#
# One FQDN per line; # comments allowed; blank lines ignored.
#
# IMPORTANT — LITERAL NAMES ONLY:
#   This list is resolved with `dig +short A <name>`. An apex name does
#   NOT cover its subdomains. "facebook.com" resolves to facebook.com's
#   A record only; "static.fbcdn.net" is a different name and needs its
#   own line. Always write the FQDNs you actually need.
#
# Only add what is BLOCKED / geo-restricted on this network. Anything
# that resolves and connects fine direct must stay out of this file —
# proxying it costs latency and can break CDNs that pin by IP.
#
# Alternate lists:
#   cp domains-myanmar.txt.example domains.txt   # broad Myanmar list
#
# NEVER ADD:
#   fonts.npmjs.com — DNS NXDOMAIN, no A record to resolve.
#   packagist.org   — IPv6-only here, resolution yields no usable IPv4.

# --- Group 1: GitHub REST API -------------------------------------------
# Why: git clone / raw / release downloads over github.com work fine
# direct on this network; only the REST API is TCP-blocked. Adding the
# web apex would route nothing useful and would slow down clones.
api.github.com

# --- Group 2: Facebook family -------------------------------------------
# Why: the whole family is TCP-blocked direct. Facebook serves content
# from many hostnames and each one is resolved literally, so they are
# listed explicitly rather than relying on the apex.
facebook.com
www.facebook.com
graph.facebook.com
upload.facebook.com
developers.facebook.com
fbcdn.net
fb.com

# --- Group 3: AI / dev tools (geo-restricted) ---------------------------
# Why: cursor.com is added to the active list for this operator's network.
# Literal FQDN only per the rule above — add any subdomain you actually
# hit on its own line.
cursor.com

# --- Group 4: OPTIONAL / geo-restricted ---------------------------------
# These resolve and connect fine DIRECT from this host, so they are
# parked here to keep the default list minimal (smaller ipset, fewer
# surprises). Uncomment the ones you actually need if you move to a
# network where they are blocked or geo-restricted (e.g. AI Studio and
# friends on some ISPs).
#aistudio.google.com
#googleapis.com
#google.com
#gstatic.com
#googleusercontent.com